WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.600
We were in a store 
and a guy in that store

2
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.300
told us to put our uniforms on.

3
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.600
"what the hell are 
you talking about?"

4
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.300
He says...

5
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.100
The USA is in 
a war with Japan.

6
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:23.800
We couldn't believe it.

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.500
Well. our country 
was attacked.

8
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:27.500
It's different.

9
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.900
It wasn't Iike 
Korea or Vietnam.

10
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:30.900
We was attacked.

11
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.500
And. you know. 
it was a feeling that...

12
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.900
maybe. we're just 
dumb country people but.

13
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:41.200
where I come from. 
but. a lot of us volunteered.

14
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.300
Who would like to 
volunteer for the tank corps?

15
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.900
Who would like to 
volunteer for the air force?

16
00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:49.900
Who would like to 
volunteer for the navy or whatever?

17
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.200
And then. they said.

18
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.800
"who would like to 
volunteer for the airborne?"

19
00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:56.300
Somebody says. 
"what the hell's the airborne?"

20
00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.900
Nobody ever heard of it.

21
00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.900
We came from a 
small. small town

22
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:03.900
and three fellas in that 
town were. that were "4f".

23
00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:07.700
committed suicide 
because they couldn't go.

24
00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.600
a different time.

25
00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.200
I did things.

26
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.900
I didn't do 'em for medals.

27
00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:13.900
I didn't do 'em for accolades.

28
00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:17.200
I did 'em because 
it's what had to be done.

29
00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.100
The guy says. 
"would you jump out of airplanes?

30
00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:21.400
"You know. 
you got all your army equipment

31
00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:24.300
and you jump out of airplanes. 
to fight the enemy."

32
00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.800
These guys. 
they said. "go to hell".

33
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:27.700
Nobody put up their hands.

34
00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:30.300
And then. I don't know 
what it was brought it up.

35
00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.900
but the guy giving 
the speech was saying.

36
00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:35.500
"but you get paid 
$50 a month more."

37
00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:38.600
So. that made it 
a hundred bucks.

38
00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.000
I want a whiff of chicken pie.

39
00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.000
Okay. boys. 
let's get this gear stowed.

40
00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.000
Fox company.

41
00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.900
we go in five.

42
00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:18.200
In the name of the father 
and the son and of the holy...

43
00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:23.800
1st platoon draw small arms.

44
00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:26.700
Do you need a hand. lieutenant?

45
00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.700
Easy company!

46
00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:31.100
Listen up!

47
00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:32.200
Gather up around me.

48
00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:35.300
Just move it up. 
c'mon. gentlemen.

49
00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.800
Let's go!

50
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:44.000
Now. the channel coast 
is socked in with rain and fog.

51
00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:46.500
High winds on the drop zone.

52
00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:48.300
No jump tonight.

53
00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:50.600
The invasion has 
been postponed.

54
00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.500
We're on a 24 hour stand-down.

55
00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:54.600
sonofabitch.

56
00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:57.300
Drill sergeants. take charge.

57
00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.900
Well. this is quite a surprise.

58
00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:02.700
Not particularly.

59
00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:05.800
It so happens 
I rather expected it

60
00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:10.900
Well. I can't see how you
 people can pass up $80.000

61
00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:12.700
for the cause.

62
00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:14.400
For whose cause?

63
00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:17.200
If you're so interested
 in serving a cause.

64
00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.500
why don't you join the army?

65
00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:22.200
Oh...

66
00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.200
I think it's clearing up.

67
00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:49.600
You think it's clearing up?

68
00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:51.100
No.

69
00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:55.000
I think it's clearing up.

70
00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.000
How are your men?

71
00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:02.000
They'll be fine.

72
00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:08.300
Five o'clock in New York.

73
00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:10.900
Four o'clock in Chicago.

74
00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.000
Happy hour. huh?

75
00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:15.100
Yeah.

76
00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.400
Happy hour.

77
00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:17.600
A couple of drinks.

78
00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:21.300
maybe an early 
dinner before the theater.

79
00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:30.200
A civilized place 
for civilized men.

80
00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:37.600
Should've been 
born earlier. Nix.

81
00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:40.200
What. and give up all this?

82
00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:58.100
We'll go to Chicago. 
I'll take you there.

83
00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:00.700
Yeah.

84
00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:03.300
We'll see.

85
00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:13.300
Actually. you know 
who's from there?

86
00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:14.200
Who?

87
00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:15.600
Oh. him.

88
00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:20.000
712 days of that 
sonofabitch and here we are.

89
00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:49.700
You people are at 
the position of attention.

90
00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:00.200
Private Perconte. have you 
been blousing your trousers

91
00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:03.100
over your boots 
like a paratrooper?

92
00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:03.600
No. sir.

93
00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.500
Then explain the 
creases at the bottom.

94
00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:06.100
No excuse. sir.

95
00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:09.300
Volunteering for the parachute 
infantry is one thing. Perconte.

96
00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:12.400
but you've got a long way 
to prove that you belong here.

97
00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:15.100
Your weekend pass is revoked.

98
00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:16.600
Name?

99
00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:18.100
Luz. George.

100
00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:21.000
Dirt in the rear side aperture.

101
00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.600
Pass revoked.

102
00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:36.900
When did you sew on 
these chevrons. sergeant Lipton?

103
00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:38.400
Yesterday. sir.

104
00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:40.500
Long enough to notice this.

105
00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:41.600
Revoked.

106
00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:42.700
Sir.

107
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:44.900
Name?

108
00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:46.800
Malarkey. Donald G.

109
00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:47.400
Malarkey?

110
00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:49.600
Malarkey's slang 
for bullshit. isn't it?

111
00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:50.800
Yes. sir.

112
00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:55.100
Rust on the butt plate 
hinge spring. private bullshit.

113
00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:57.700
Revoked.

114
00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:58.600
Name?

115
00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:01.200
Liebgott. Joseph D. sir.

116
00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.400
Rusty bayonet. Liebgott.

117
00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:07.100
You wanna kill Germans?

118
00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:08.000
Yes. sir.

119
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.600
Not with this.

120
00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:14.300
I wouldn't take this 
rusty piece of shit to war.

121
00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:17.800
and I will not take you 
to war in your condition.

122
00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:20.000
Now. thanks to these 
men and their infractions.

123
00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:23.700
every man in the company 
who had a weekend pass.

124
00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:26.400
has lost it.

125
00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:31.500
Change into your pt gear. 
we're running currahee.

126
00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:35.900
2nd platoon fall out.

127
00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:37.100
We have two minutes.

128
00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:39.700
Fall out!

129
00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.900
I ain't going up that hill.

130
00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:47.500
Hey. Perconte. 
what are you thinking of.

131
00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:48.800
blousin' your pants?

132
00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:51.300
Shut up. Martin. alright?

133
00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:51.900
He gigged everybody.

134
00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:53.300
Yeah. well. 
you should know better.

135
00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:55.200
Don't give him no excuses.

136
00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:55.900
Excuses?

137
00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:57.800
Why don't you come here. 
look at these trousers.

138
00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:59.700
get down and you tell me 
if there's a crease on 'em?

139
00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:02.400
Alright. let's go. 
on the road in pt formation.

140
00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:04.700
Let's move. move. move!

141
00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:07.400
Perconte. let's go. Perconte.

142
00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:14.500
Private white. 
why are you not in your pt gear?

143
00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:20.800
I asked you a question. private.

144
00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:39.500
Oh. Easy company.

145
00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:40.800
and while you're running. 
don't worry.

146
00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:42.900
we'll take your dames 
to the movies for you.

147
00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:46.600
Yeah. good. they need 
some female company.

148
00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.000
Where do we run?

149
00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:53.700
Currahee.

150
00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:55.600
And what does 
"Currahee" mean?

151
00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:56.700
We stand alone.

152
00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:58.200
How far up. 
how far down?

153
00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:00.500
Three miles up. 
three miles down.

154
00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:02.600
And what company is this?

155
00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:03.900
Easy company.

156
00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:05.200
And what do we do?

157
00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:06.100
Stand alone.

158
00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:07.800
Do not help that man!

159
00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:09.400
Do not help that man.

160
00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:12.200
We do not stop.

161
00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:15.600
You've got 30 minutes to 
get to the top of this mountain

162
00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:18.800
If you wanna serve 
in the paratroopers.

163
00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:21.400
Hi-ho. Silver!

164
00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:49.400
C'mon. you can make it up there.

165
00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:49.800
C'mon.

166
00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:51.400
C'mon now. c'mon. 
Alley. let's go.

167
00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:52.100
C'mon. Guarnere.

168
00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:53.100
Christenson. c'mon.

169
00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:55.800
I never thought I'd see 
the day. private Wynn.

170
00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:58.400
We are coming on 23 minutes.

171
00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:02.700
That may be good enough 
for the rest of the 506.

172
00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:06.700
but that is not good 
enough for Easy company.

173
00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:19.600
We can make it. 
we can do this. c'mon.

174
00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:49.900
I'm gonna say something.

175
00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:52.500
To who?

176
00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:56.500
Lieutenant Winters.

177
00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:58.100
What is it?

178
00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:00.800
Permission to speak. sir?

179
00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:02.000
Permission granted.

180
00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:04.700
Sir. we got nine companies. sir.

181
00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:07.300
That we do.

182
00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:09.100
Well. how come 
we're the only company

183
00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:11.900
marching every friday night. 
12 miles. full pack.

184
00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:13.300
in the pitch dark?

185
00:14:13.300 --> 00:14:15.300
Why do you think. 
private Randleman?

186
00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:18.100
Lieutenant Sobel hates us. sir.

187
00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:25.500
Lieutenant Sobel does 
not hate Easy company.

188
00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:27.500
private Randleman.

189
00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:30.100
He just hates you.

190
00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:32.700
Thank you. sir.

191
00:14:34.300 --> 00:14:35.100
He hates him back.

192
00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:37.700
He hates you too. Muck.

193
00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:40.100
Lieutenant Winters. 
I want canteens out of belts

194
00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:41.000
With the caps unscrewed.

195
00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:42.900
Easy company. 
canteens out and open.

196
00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:46.400
On my command. they will 
pour the contents onto the ground.

197
00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:49.600
On the co's order. 
you will upend your canteen.

198
00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:50.800
Now. lieutenant.

199
00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:53.400
Pour 'em.

200
00:14:58.200 --> 00:14:59.600
Who is this?

201
00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:00.600
Christenson.

202
00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:03.400
Why is there no 
water in your canteen?

203
00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:06.100
You drank from your 
canteen. didn't you?

204
00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:06.700
Sir. I...

205
00:15:06.700 --> 00:15:07.700
Lieutenant Winters.

206
00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:08.300
Yes. sir.

207
00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:10.200
Was this man ordered 
to not drink from his canteen

208
00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:12.700
during the friday night march?

209
00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:13.400
He was. sir.

210
00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:15.500
Private Christenson. 
you have disobeyed a direct order.

211
00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:16.700
You will fill your canteen

212
00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:21.100
and repeat all 12 miles 
of the march immediately.

213
00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:22.100
Yes. sir.

214
00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:24.700
Fall out!

215
00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:34.100
What in the name of god 
are you doing with my company?

216
00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:36.500
You're late and you allow troopers

217
00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:38.600
to disobey direct orders?

218
00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:40.400
No excuse. sir.

219
00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:43.800
You're making me 
look bad. lieutenant.

220
00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:46.600
This is not Dog company.

221
00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:48.800
This is not Fox company.

222
00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:50.600
This. this is Easy company.

223
00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:53.200
And under my command. 
this will be the first

224
00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:56.500
and finest company 
in this regiment.

225
00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:59.700
I want the names of six men.

226
00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:01.200
their infractions

227
00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:03.700
and your disciplinary 
recommendations

228
00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:05.800
on my desk by 0130.

229
00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:07.300
Is that clear?

230
00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:10.000
What infractions. sir?

231
00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:13.000
Find some.

232
00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:17.600
So. what'd you do?

233
00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:20.900
Picked six men and 
gave 'em latrine duty.

234
00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:22.400
The lucky six?

235
00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:24.800
McDonald. Toye. Perconte.

236
00:16:24.800 --> 00:16:25.800
Lipton.

237
00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:29.500
Muck and Guarnere.

238
00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:30.600
Why them?

239
00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:31.800
It was their turn.

240
00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:33.600
Sobel's a genius.

241
00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:37.400
I had a headmaster just 
like him in prep school.

242
00:16:37.400 --> 00:16:38.400
I know the type.

243
00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:39.300
Lewis.

244
00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:42.300
Michelangelo's a genius. 
Beethoven's a genius.

245
00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:43.500
You know a man 
in this company

246
00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:46.100
who wouldn't double-time 
Currahee with a full pack

247
00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:49.700
just to piss in that 
guy's morning coffee?

248
00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:52.400
Let's go. let's go.

249
00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:55.800
Stand in the door.

250
00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:56.300
Go.

251
00:16:56.300 --> 00:16:57.600
One thousand. 
two thousand.

252
00:16:57.600 --> 00:17:00.400
You just broke both 
your legs. private Gordon.

253
00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:03.000
Are you trying to 
get yourself killed?

254
00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.100
No. sir.

255
00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:07.300
Stand in the door.

256
00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:23.600
Shit.

257
00:17:27.300 --> 00:17:29.500
To the wall. 
to the wall.

258
00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:30.100
Over as a team.

259
00:17:30.100 --> 00:17:32.300
Go on. 
against the wall.

260
00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:34.800
Jesus. what the hell is this?

261
00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:37.500
That's pig guts. boy.

262
00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:42.900
Goddammit!

263
00:17:43.900 --> 00:17:46.200
Why are you here. 
private Gordon?

264
00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:47.900
I wanna be in 
the airborne. sir.

265
00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:48.500
I don't believe you.

266
00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.000
Why are you here. 
private Gordon?

267
00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:51.400
I wanna be in 
the airborne. sir.

268
00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:53.200
You have 50 minutes 
to the top and back.

269
00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:55.700
and I will be watching you.

270
00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:58.300
What are you waiting for?

271
00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:42.000
Easy company has the 
finest performance record

272
00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:44.200
in the entire 2nd battalion.

273
00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:47.700
I believe every bit of 
that is thanks to you.

274
00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:50.500
Congratulations. 
captain Sobel.

275
00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:51.100
Thank you. sir.

276
00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:56.300
Isn't that lieutenant Winters 
leading Easy company in pt?

277
00:18:56.800 --> 00:18:58.200
Yes. sir.

278
00:18:58.200 --> 00:18:59.300
He's a damned good man.

279
00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:02.600
I was planning on giving 
him a set of these today.

280
00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:03.900
Why don't you do it?

281
00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:06.900
He'd be proud to 
get 'em from you.

282
00:19:11.700 --> 00:19:14.300
Pornography. 
contraband.

283
00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:20.800
Non-regulation clothing. 
contraband.

284
00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:25.000
This man had 200 prophylactic 
kits in his footlocker.

285
00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:28.500
How in the name of god was 
he gonna have the strength

286
00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:31.200
to fight the war?

287
00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:33.100
How is it private. 
private Tipper

288
00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:36.900
Has spare time for so 
much correspondence?

289
00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:42.900
Captain. are personal letters 
to be considered contraband?

290
00:19:42.900 --> 00:19:46.200
These men aren't 
paratroopers yet. lieutenant.

291
00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:49.100
They have no personal property.

292
00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:54.400
What is this?

293
00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:55.600
Anybody?

294
00:19:56.100 --> 00:19:58.500
Er. it's a can of peaches. sir.

295
00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:02.500
Lieutenant Nixon thinks 
this is a can of peaches.

296
00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:05.000
That is incorrect. lieutenant.

297
00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:06.500
Your weekend pass 
is cancelled.

298
00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:09.700
This is United States 
Army property

299
00:20:10.900 --> 00:20:14.200
Which was taken. 
without authorization.

300
00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:15.600
from my mess facility.

301
00:20:15.600 --> 00:20:19.500
and I will not tolerate 
thievery in my unit.

302
00:20:19.500 --> 00:20:21.300
Whose footlocker is this?

303
00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:23.900
Private Parkes. sir.

304
00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:26.800
Get rid of him.

305
00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:29.200
All weekend passes 
are cancelled.

306
00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:31.800
Officers included.

307
00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:35.900
Carry on.

308
00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:41.500
Lieutenant Winters.

309
00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:50.500
Colonel sink has 
seen fit to promote you.

310
00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:55.300
As 1st lieutenant. 
you'll serve as my executive officer.

311
00:20:55.300 --> 00:20:57.000
Congratulations.

312
00:20:57.700 --> 00:20:59.300
Thank you. sir.

313
00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:03.300
And. as a test of your 
organizational skills

314
00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:05.900
and command potential.

315
00:21:05.900 --> 00:21:08.400
I am designating you...

316
00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:10.500
mess officer for 14 days.

317
00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:14.100
Report to the mess 
kitchen at 0515 hours.

318
00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:17.600
Company breakfast 
to be served at 0600.

319
00:21:18.600 --> 00:21:21.200
Yes. sir.

320
00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:22.500
Oh. and. Dick...

321
00:21:22.500 --> 00:21:24.500
There's rain forecast tomorrow.

322
00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:28.100
So the company will 
have a light afternoon

323
00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:31.400
