change of pace.

326
00:21:38.300 --> 00:21:39.700
Would you agree?

327
00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:40.700
Yes. sir.

328
00:21:40.700 --> 00:21:43.300
I like spaghetti.

329
00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:54.300
Hold on. 
more coming.

330
00:21:54.300 --> 00:21:57.200
These guys are packing it away.

331
00:22:08.100 --> 00:22:09.000
This stuff is orange.

332
00:22:09.000 --> 00:22:11.700
Spaghetti ain't 
supposed to be orange.

333
00:22:11.700 --> 00:22:12.600
This ain't spaghetti.

334
00:22:12.600 --> 00:22:15.200
This is army noodles 
with ketchup.

335
00:22:15.200 --> 00:22:17.000
You ain't gotta eat it.

336
00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:19.800
Oh. c'mon. Gonorrhea. 
as a fellow Italian.

337
00:22:19.800 --> 00:22:22.000
you should know that 
calling this crap spaghetti

338
00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:22.800
is a mortal sin.

339
00:22:22.800 --> 00:22:24.300
You don't want it. 
I'll have it.

340
00:22:24.300 --> 00:22:25.600
No. no. no. 
I'm eating here.

341
00:22:25.600 --> 00:22:27.700
Hey. get outta here.

342
00:22:27.700 --> 00:22:30.000
Orders changed. get up!

343
00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.200
Lectures are cancelled.

344
00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:34.600
Easy company is 
running up Currahee.

345
00:22:34.600 --> 00:22:37.200
Move. move!

346
00:22:38.100 --> 00:22:41.100
Three miles up. 
three miles down.

347
00:22:41.900 --> 00:22:44.500
Hi-ho. Silver!

348
00:22:45.400 --> 00:22:48.100
Let's go. 
let's go.

349
00:22:50.200 --> 00:22:53.000
You're a washout. 
private Hoobler!

350
00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:56.300
You should pack up both 
your ears and go home.

351
00:22:56.300 --> 00:22:57.800
Looks like Gordon's done.

352
00:22:57.800 --> 00:22:59.500
Aren't you. Gordon. 
you finished?

353
00:22:59.500 --> 00:23:02.000
You do not deserve 
to get your wings.

354
00:23:02.000 --> 00:23:03.100
Private Randleman. 
you look tired.

355
00:23:03.100 --> 00:23:07.700
There's an ambulance waiting 
for you at the bottom of the hill.

356
00:23:07.700 --> 00:23:09.900
It can all be over right now.

357
00:23:09.900 --> 00:23:12.800
No more pain. 
no more Currahee.

358
00:23:13.400 --> 00:23:14.400
No more captain Sobel.

359
00:23:14.400 --> 00:23:18.400
We pull upon the risers. 
we fall upon the grass.

360
00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:21.200
we never land upon our feet. 
we always hit our ass.

361
00:23:21.200 --> 00:23:25.000
Aye. aye. Christ almighty. 
who the hell are we.

362
00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:28.200
zim-zam. goddamn. 
we're airborne infantry.

363
00:23:28.200 --> 00:23:32.200
We pull upon the risers. 
we fall upon the grass.

364
00:23:32.200 --> 00:23:35.300
we never land upon our feet. 
we always hit our ass.

365
00:23:35.300 --> 00:23:38.800
Aye. aye. Christ almighty. 
who the hell are we.

366
00:23:38.800 --> 00:23:42.500
zim-zam. goddamn. 
we're airborne infantry.

367
00:23:54.800 --> 00:23:58.800
So. do we feel like we're 
ready to be army paratroopers?

368
00:23:58.900 --> 00:24:00.500
Yes. sergeant.

369
00:24:00.500 --> 00:24:01.100
I hope so.

370
00:24:01.100 --> 00:24:05.600
This'll be the first of five 
exits from a c47 aircraft

371
00:24:05.600 --> 00:24:07.100
scheduled for today.

372
00:24:07.100 --> 00:24:08.400
Get ready.

373
00:24:08.400 --> 00:24:11.100
Stand up.

374
00:24:11.700 --> 00:24:12.200
Hook up.

375
00:24:12.200 --> 00:24:15.600
Upon successful completion 
of your fifth and final jump.

376
00:24:15.600 --> 00:24:18.200
you'll be certified 
army paratroopers.

377
00:24:18.200 --> 00:24:20.800
Check equipment!

378
00:24:21.800 --> 00:24:24.900
Sound-off for 
equipment check!

379
00:24:24.900 --> 00:24:26.200
Nine okay.

380
00:24:26.200 --> 00:24:27.400
Eight okay.

381
00:24:27.400 --> 00:24:28.700
Seven okay.

382
00:24:28.700 --> 00:24:29.900
Six okay.

383
00:24:30.400 --> 00:24:31.600
Five okay.

384
00:24:32.600 --> 00:24:33.800
Four okay.

385
00:24:34.100 --> 00:24:35.600
Three okay.

386
00:24:35.600 --> 00:24:36.600
Two okay.

387
00:24:36.600 --> 00:24:37.100
One okay.

388
00:24:37.100 --> 00:24:39.400
There'll be a lot of men 
dropping from the sky today.

389
00:24:39.400 --> 00:24:42.600
Hopefully. under 
deployed canopies.

390
00:24:44.100 --> 00:24:46.700
Stand in the door!

391
00:24:47.500 --> 00:24:50.900
I guarantee you're 
gonna love it. lieutenant.

392
00:24:50.900 --> 00:24:52.200
Go. go!

393
00:24:52.200 --> 00:24:53.600
Jumping from 1000 feet

394
00:24:54.400 --> 00:24:57.200
