433
00:27:45.700 --> 00:27:49.300
But by God. the 506 is gonna 
forge that brand new concept

434
00:27:49.300 --> 00:27:50.900
into victory.

435
00:27:50.900 --> 00:27:51.300
Yes. sir.

436
00:27:51.300 --> 00:27:53.600
I want you to know 
that I'm damned proud

437
00:27:53.600 --> 00:27:55.200
of each and every one of you.

438
00:27:55.200 --> 00:27:57.800
Now. you deserve this party.

439
00:27:58.200 --> 00:27:59.700
Thank you. 
sergeant Grant.

440
00:27:59.700 --> 00:28:00.200
sir.

441
00:28:00.200 --> 00:28:02.000
So. I want you to have fun...

442
00:28:02.000 --> 00:28:04.200
and remember our motto...

443
00:28:04.200 --> 00:28:08.300
Currahee!

444
00:28:34.500 --> 00:28:35.400
Petty.

445
00:28:35.700 --> 00:28:36.500
Map.

446
00:28:36.800 --> 00:28:37.800
C'mon.

447
00:28:38.900 --> 00:28:41.600
Ah. Christ.

448
00:28:51.700 --> 00:28:54.300
We're in the wrong position.

449
00:28:57.700 --> 00:28:58.800
We're in the wrong position.

450
00:28:58.800 --> 00:29:01.300
We're textbook 
position for ambush. sir.

451
00:29:01.300 --> 00:29:02.400
We should sit tight.

452
00:29:02.400 --> 00:29:04.500
let the enemy team 
come into our killing zone.

453
00:29:04.500 --> 00:29:06.200
They're right out 
there somewhere.

454
00:29:06.200 --> 00:29:07.500
Let's just get 'em.

455
00:29:07.500 --> 00:29:09.400
Sir. we have 
perfect cover here.

456
00:29:09.400 --> 00:29:12.300
Lieutenant. 
deploy your troops.

457
00:29:14.800 --> 00:29:16.100
2nd platoon.

458
00:29:16.100 --> 00:29:17.300
move out.

459
00:29:17.800 --> 00:29:18.900
What?

460
00:29:18.900 --> 00:29:21.500
Tactical column.

461
00:29:38.700 --> 00:29:39.900
Captain. 
you've just been killed.

462
00:29:39.900 --> 00:29:43.400
along with 95% 
of your company.

463
00:29:43.400 --> 00:29:44.900
Your outfit?

464
00:29:45.200 --> 00:29:48.500
Easy company. 
2nd battalion 506th.

465
00:29:51.700 --> 00:29:54.000
Leave three wounded 
men on the ground

466
00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:57.300
and report back to 
the assembly area.

467
00:29:57.300 --> 00:30:00.000
Goddammit.

468
00:30:04.000 --> 00:30:06.600
You. you. you.

469
00:30:09.300 --> 00:30:10.300
Well. what are you gonna do?

470
00:30:10.300 --> 00:30:13.600
Nothing. just keep 
training the men.

471
00:30:14.900 --> 00:30:17.500
Am I interrupting?

472
00:30:18.500 --> 00:30:19.500
No. no.

473
00:30:19.500 --> 00:30:21.200
Lieutenant Lewis Nixon.

474
00:30:21.200 --> 00:30:24.400
Lieutenant Harry Welsh. 
just in from the 82nd.

475
00:30:24.400 --> 00:30:26.100
Congratulations on the promotion.

476
00:30:26.100 --> 00:30:27.800
Ah. thanks. 
if you wanna call it that.

477
00:30:27.800 --> 00:30:30.200
You'll learn him pretty quickly.

478
00:30:30.200 --> 00:30:32.300
No flaws. no vices. 
no sense of humor.

479
00:30:32.300 --> 00:30:36.200
Just like your chums 
up at battalion staff.

480
00:30:36.200 --> 00:30:37.500
What's up?

481
00:30:37.500 --> 00:30:40.400
I'm hearing a lot of rumblings.

482
00:30:40.800 --> 00:30:41.600
Sobel?

483
00:30:41.600 --> 00:30:43.200
Just talking about that.

484
00:30:43.200 --> 00:30:46.900
So. he gets a little 
jumpy in the field?

485
00:30:46.900 --> 00:30:47.300
hmm-mmm.

486
00:30:47.300 --> 00:30:49.100
He gets jumpy and 
then you get killed.

487
00:30:49.100 --> 00:30:50.200
That's nice.

488
00:30:50.200 --> 00:30:52.500
Yeah. listen. 
if we discuss it.

489
00:30:52.500 --> 00:30:55.300
I think it should just 
be amongst ourselves.

490
00:30:55.300 --> 00:30:57.900
Oh. absolutely.

491
00:31:03.700 --> 00:31:06.300
2nd platoon ready?

492
00:31:06.300 --> 00:31:07.200
Ready. sir.

493
00:31:07.200 --> 00:31:09.600
Then get them in formation.

494
00:31:09.600 --> 00:31:11.200
We're moving out.

495
00:31:11.200 --> 00:31:13.800
Yes. sir.

496
00:31:36.900 --> 00:31:38.500
Shut up. Cobb.

497
00:31:39.200 --> 00:31:40.700
Eh. you gotta admit it.

498
00:31:40.700 --> 00:31:41.900
He's got no chance.

499
00:31:41.900 --> 00:31:44.200
Either the krauts will get him.

500
00:31:44.200 --> 00:31:45.700
or one of us.

501
00:31:46.000 --> 00:31:47.000
Who. Sobel?

502
00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:49.200
He screwed up one maneuver.

503
00:31:49.200 --> 00:31:51.800
Well. you know. 
I'm always fumbling with grenades.

504
00:31:51.800 --> 00:31:55.200
It would be easy if one 
went off by accident. you know?

505
00:31:55.200 --> 00:31:58.300
Well. now they must have 
put him in charge for a reason.

506
00:31:58.300 --> 00:32:03.500
Yeah. 'cause the army wouldn't 
make a mistake. right. Shift?

507
00:32:18.100 --> 00:32:19.600
Going my way?

508
00:32:19.600 --> 00:32:20.900
Wherever the train takes me.

509
00:32:20.900 --> 00:32:22.400
Where do you 
suppose that might be?

510
00:32:22.400 --> 00:32:23.300
I haven't got a clue.

511
00:32:23.300 --> 00:32:24.700
Yeah. c'mon. 
take a guess.

512
00:32:24.700 --> 00:32:27.300
Atlantic. Pacific. 
Atlantic?

513
00:32:27.300 --> 00:32:29.900
I'm not the intelligence officer.

514
00:32:29.900 --> 00:32:30.300
mmm.

515
00:32:30.300 --> 00:32:34.700
Well. as such. I of course know. 
but if I told you.

516
00:32:34.700 --> 00:32:35.900
I'd have to kill you.

517
00:32:35.900 --> 00:32:38.500
So. don't tell me.

518
00:32:40.300 --> 00:32:41.500
New York city.

519
00:32:41.500 --> 00:32:42.900
Troop ship.

520
00:32:42.900 --> 00:32:45.500
England.

521
00:32:46.800 --> 00:32:49.800
We're invading Europe. 
my friend.

522
00:32:50.100 --> 00:32:52.800
Fortress Europa.

523
00:32:53.500 --> 00:32:56.100
Since when do I drink?

524
00:32:56.800 --> 00:33:01.600
If I thought you'd drink it. 
I wouldn't offer it to you.

525
00:33:02.600 --> 00:33:03.400
Nix?

526
00:33:03.400 --> 00:33:07.400
What are you gonna do 
when you get into combat?

527
00:33:08.200 --> 00:33:12.200
Oh. I have every confidence 
in my scrounging abilities.

528
00:33:12.300 --> 00:33:17.000
And I have a case of vat 69 
hidden in your footlocker.

529
00:33:21.300 --> 00:33:22.300
Really?

530
00:33:23.000 --> 00:33:24.200
Oh. yeah.

531
00:33:25.500 --> 00:33:26.600
Morning.

532
00:33:27.900 --> 00:33:28.300
mmm.

533
00:33:28.300 --> 00:33:31.600
This could turn into 
a real nice trip.

534
00:33:47.300 --> 00:33:48.700
"Dear sir or madam.

535
00:33:48.700 --> 00:33:51.200
soon your son will 
drop from the sky

536
00:33:51.200 --> 00:33:53.800
to engage and 
defeat the enemy.

537
00:33:53.800 --> 00:33:57.200
Your frequent letters of 
love and encouragement

538
00:33:57.200 --> 00:33:59.500
will arm him with 
a fighting heart.

539
00:33:59.500 --> 00:34:04.000
With that he cannot fail. 
