such a school than you are.

804
00:50:29.800 --> 00:50:32.400
Sir?

805
00:50:33.700 --> 00:50:37.200
I'm reassigning you 
to Chilton Foliat.

806
00:50:45.200 --> 00:50:48.000
I'm losing Easy company?

807
00:50:48.000 --> 00:50:51.200
The war effort 
needs you elsewhere.

808
00:50:56.800 --> 00:50:59.600
Permission to speak. sir?

809
00:50:59.600 --> 00:51:02.200
Granted.

810
00:51:03.900 --> 00:51:06.600
Is. who. 
who will be replacing me?

811
00:51:06.600 --> 00:51:10.600
Lieutenant Meehan 
from Baker company is senior.

812
00:51:12.400 --> 00:51:14.800
Good luck at 
Chilton Foliat. Herbert.

813
00:51:14.800 --> 00:51:17.500
Don't let us down now.

814
00:51:23.700 --> 00:51:26.300
No. sir.

815
00:51:31.400 --> 00:51:34.100
Carry on.

816
00:52:26.600 --> 00:52:27.800
2nd platoon. listen up.

817
00:52:27.800 --> 00:52:31.200
I want the 1st squad 
and a-side tents right up there.

818
00:52:31.200 --> 00:52:33.800
3rd squad. second row...

819
00:52:48.800 --> 00:52:50.200
Holy shit.

820
00:52:50.200 --> 00:52:53.600
No. it's all right. 
mate. we're tommies.

821
00:52:53.600 --> 00:52:54.800
not bleedin' bosch.

822
00:52:54.800 --> 00:52:56.400
Is all this real?

823
00:52:56.400 --> 00:52:57.200
Yeah. yeah.

824
00:52:57.200 --> 00:52:58.600
Well. some of it's 
from the hermans.

825
00:52:58.600 --> 00:52:59.800
that somebody's 
tailors knocked up.

826
00:52:59.800 --> 00:53:01.300
for you lads. actually. 
so. you can get your mince pies

827
00:53:01.300 --> 00:53:04.400
on some of this jerry clobber. 
if you know what I mean.

828
00:53:04.400 --> 00:53:05.700
Not really.

829
00:53:06.100 --> 00:53:06.600
Eh?

830
00:53:06.600 --> 00:53:07.600
Hey. mac. you got a luger?

831
00:53:07.600 --> 00:53:09.700
I'm dying to get my 
hands on a real luger.

832
00:53:09.700 --> 00:53:11.500
Yeah. go on then.

833
00:53:12.100 --> 00:53:14.700
Quick butchers. yeah?

834
00:53:18.300 --> 00:53:20.300
Boy. she sure is a doozy.

835
00:53:20.300 --> 00:53:22.000
Yeah. it's pukka. innit.

836
00:53:22.000 --> 00:53:22.800
What?

837
00:53:22.800 --> 00:53:25.500
Hey. Petty.

838
00:53:26.300 --> 00:53:27.500
Hey. mate.

839
00:53:28.300 --> 00:53:32.300
You're having a bath if you 
think you're half-inching that.

840
00:53:32.300 --> 00:53:33.400
Oh. yeah.

841
00:53:34.000 --> 00:53:34.900
Sorry.

842
00:53:35.500 --> 00:53:36.400
Well. good luck.

843
00:53:36.400 --> 00:53:38.900
You too. mate.

844
00:53:38.900 --> 00:53:40.300
What's up. Hoobs?

845
00:53:40.300 --> 00:53:42.700
These men have been 
through the toughest training

846
00:53:42.700 --> 00:53:44.300
the army has to offer.

847
00:53:44.300 --> 00:53:46.800
Under the worst 
possible circumstances.

848
00:53:46.800 --> 00:53:49.300
And they volunteered for it.

849
00:53:49.300 --> 00:53:52.600
Christ. Dick. I was just 
shooting craps with them.

850
00:53:52.600 --> 00:53:53.400
It's not like...

851
00:53:53.400 --> 00:53:54.600
You know why 
they volunteered?

852
00:53:54.600 --> 00:53:57.300
So. when things got really 
bad the man in the foxhole

853
00:53:57.300 --> 00:53:59.400
next to them would be the best.

854
00:53:59.400 --> 00:54:03.000
Not some draftee who's 
gonna get him killed.

855
00:54:03.000 --> 00:54:04.500
Are you ticked 
because they like me?

856
00:54:04.500 --> 00:54:07.500
Because I'm spending time 
to get to know my soldiers?

857
00:54:07.500 --> 00:54:10.300
I mean. c'mon. you've been 
with these guys for. what.

858
00:54:10.300 --> 00:54:11.000
two years?

859
00:54:11.000 --> 00:54:12.800
I've been here for six days.

860
00:54:12.800 --> 00:54:14.900
You're gambling. Bob.

861
00:54:14.900 --> 00:54:17.000
So what. soldiers do that.

862
00:54:17.000 --> 00:54:19.700
I don't deserve 
a reprimand for it.

863
00:54:19.700 --> 00:54:22.300
What if you'd won?

864
00:54:22.600 --> 00:54:23.600
What?

865
00:54:23.800 --> 00:54:26.600
What-if-you'd-won?

866
00:54:31.100 --> 00:54:32.400
Never put yourself in a position

867
00:54:32.400 --> 00:54:35.500
where you can take 
from these men.

868
00:54:40.300 --> 00:54:41.600
Lieutenant Meehan?

869
00:54:41.600 --> 00:54:42.600
Enter.

870
00:54:44.000 --> 00:54:47.700
On the last training jump. 
I had a compass.

871
00:54:48.100 --> 00:54:50.700
Close the flap.

872
00:54:52.900 --> 00:54:54.800
Then we turn left.

873
00:54:54.800 --> 00:54:55.500
Yeah.

874
00:54:55.500 --> 00:54:57.600
Bearing zero four two.

875
00:54:57.600 --> 00:54:58.900
12 minutes.

876
00:54:59.600 --> 00:55:01.300
Then another left?

877
00:55:01.300 --> 00:55:02.100
Yes.

878
00:55:02.100 --> 00:55:02.800
Yeah.

879
00:55:02.800 --> 00:55:04.300
Call it three five eight.

880
00:55:04.300 --> 00:55:06.900
for 10 and a half minutes.

881
00:55:07.100 --> 00:55:10.100
Green light. 
right over Ramsbury.

882
00:55:10.900 --> 00:55:11.900
Ramsbury.

883
00:55:11.900 --> 00:55:13.400
Every single time.

884
00:55:13.400 --> 00:55:16.900
Linear distance on 
the grid of about...

885
00:55:20.300 --> 00:55:21.200
Okay.

886
00:55:21.900 --> 00:55:22.800
Ramsbury.

887
00:55:22.800 --> 00:55:25.400
Upottery.

888
00:55:33.500 --> 00:55:34.300
So...

889
00:55:34.500 --> 00:55:37.200
It's Normandy.

890
00:55:38.200 --> 00:55:39.800
st. Marie du Mont.

891
00:55:39.800 --> 00:55:41.200
Causeway number one.

892
00:55:41.200 --> 00:55:42.600
Causeway number two.

893
00:55:42.600 --> 00:55:44.500
The ultimate field problem.

894
00:55:44.500 --> 00:55:47.200
The estuary of the Douve river

895
00:55:47.700 --> 00:55:51.100
divides two beachheads. 
code-named Utah. here.

896
00:55:51.100 --> 00:55:52.400
and Omaha. here.

897
00:55:52.400 --> 00:55:56.000
Seaborne infantry will 
hit these beaches in force

898
00:55:56.000 --> 00:55:58.700
at a date and time 
to be specified.

899
00:55:58.700 --> 00:56:00.200
h-hour. d-day.

900
00:56:00.900 --> 00:56:02.700
Airborne's objective. 
gentlemen.

901
00:56:02.700 --> 00:56:04.900
is to take the town of Careltan. 
or Carentan.

902
00:56:04.900 --> 00:56:09.600
thus linking Utah and Omaha 
into a single continuous beachhead.

903
00:56:09.600 --> 00:56:12.600
...linking Omah and Utah into 
one continuous beachhead.

904
00:56:12.600 --> 00:56:15.700
Each trooper will learn 
this operation by heart

905
00:56:15.700 --> 00:56:19.100
and know his and 
every other outfits' mission

906
00:56:19.100 --> 00:56:20.700
to the detail.

907
00:56:20.700 --> 00:56:21.900
Lieutenant Meehan?

908
00:56:21.900 --> 00:56:22.500
Yes. dukeman.

909
00:56:22.500 --> 00:56:23.600
Sir. are we dropping tonight?

910
00:56:23.600 --> 00:56:25.500
When it's time for you to know. 
we'll let you know.

911
00:56:25.500 --> 00:56:29.100
In the meantime. 
study these sand tables. maps.

912
00:56:29.100 --> 00:56:29.800
and reconnaissance photos

913
00:56:29.800 --> 00:56:32.500
until you can draw a map 
of the area by memory.

914
00:56:32.500 --> 00:56:35.000
Now. we will drop 
behind this Atlantic wall

915
00:56:35.000 --> 00:56:39.000
five hours before the 
4th infantry lands at Utah.

916
00:56:39.200 --> 00:56:43.500
And between our assembly 
area and the battalion's objective.

917
00:56:43.500 --> 00:56:44.900
there is a German garrison

918
00:56:44.900 --> 00:56:47.400
right here in this area. 
st. Marie du Mont.

919
00:56:47.400 --> 00:56:51.200
Easy company will 
destroy that garrison.

920
00:56:53.200 --> 00:56:57.200
Three day supply of k-rations. 
chocolate bars. charms candy.

921
00:56:57.300 --> 00:56:59.200
powdered coffee. 
sugar. and matches.

922
00:56:59.200 --> 00:57:01.800
Compass. bayonet. 
entrenching tool.

923
00:57:01.800 --> 00:57:03.100
ammunition. gas mask.

924
00:57:03.100 --> 00:57:07.100
Musette bag with ammo. 
my webbing. my .45. canteen.

925
00:57:07.300 --> 00:57:08.900
two cartons of smokes.

926
00:57:08.900 --> 00:57:11.300
Hawkins mine. 
two grenades.

927
00:57:11.300 --> 00:57:12.700
smoke grenade. 
gamma grenade.

928
00:57:12.700 --> 00:57:14.000
tnt. this bullshit.

929
00:57:14.000 --> 00:57:16.600
and a pair of nasty skivvies.

930
00:57:16.600 --> 00:57:17.200
What's your point?

931
00:57:17.200 --> 00:57:19.100
You know. this stuff 
weighs as much as I do.

932
00:57:19.100 --> 00:57:21.000
I've still got my chute. 
my reserve chute.

933
00:57:21.000 --> 00:57:21.600
my mae west. 
my m-1.

934
00:57:21.600 --> 00:57:23.400
Where are you keeping 
your brass knuckles?

935
00:57:23.400 --> 00:57:26.400
I could use some 
brass knuckles.

936
00:57:26.900 --> 00:57:28.100
Sergeant Martin.

937
00:57:28.100 --> 00:57:30.000
Hey. Vest. 
anything for me?

938
00:57:30.000 --> 00:57:30.800
No.

939
00:57:30.800 --> 00:57:33.400
Sergeant Martin.

940
00:57:38.700 --> 00:57:41.300
For Talbert.

941
00:57:44.800 --> 00:57:46.100
Your condoms?

942
00:57:46.100 --> 00:57:47.800
I don't know. probably.

943
00:57:47.800 --> 00:57:48.300
What you got?

944
00:57:48.300 --> 00:57:50.600
"Dear Floyd. give 'em hell."

945
00:57:50.600 --> 00:57:53.400
It's from chief of the 
Kokomo police department.

946
00:57:53.400 --> 00:57:56.100
Right.

947
00:57:56.300 --> 00:57:59.000
Whoa. you've gotta love cops.

948
00:57:59.400 --> 00:58:01.000
Alright. listen up. listen up.

949
00:58:01.000 --> 00:58:05.400
If you did not sign your 
GI life insurance policy.

950
00:58:05.800 --> 00:58:09.100
you go on over 
and see sergeant Evans

951
00:58:09.400 --> 00:58:11.300
at the headquarters 
company tent.

952
00:58:11.300 --> 00:58:14.000
You boys don't 
let your families

953
00:58:14.000 --> 00:58:15.800
miss out on $10.000.

954
00:58:15.800 --> 00:58:18.400
You hear that. Gerry?

955
00:58:18.900 --> 00:58:19.900
Hey. Lip?

956
00:58:19.900 --> 00:58:21.100
Yeah. boy.

957
00:58:22.200 --> 00:58:25.500
Has Guarnere said anything 
to you about his brother?

958
00:58:25.500 --> 00:58:26.200
No.

959
00:58:26.500 --> 00:58:27.200
I got a problem.

960
00:58:27.200 --> 00:58:29.700
My wife keeps up 
with things back home.

961
00:58:29.700 --> 00:58:31.700
casualty lists and like that.

962
00:58:31.700 --> 00:58:32.200
Yeah?

963
00:58:32.200 --> 00:58:34.600
Guarnere's brother in Italy?

964
00:58:34.600 --> 00:58:35.400
Henry?

965
00:58:35.400 --> 00:58:37.600
Killed in Monte Cassino.

966
00:58:37.600 --> 00:58:40.500
Well. I'm sure he doesn't know.

967
00:58:41.100 --> 00:58:41.900
Damn.

968
00:58:41.900 --> 00:58:43.400
What'd you think I should do?

969
00:58:43.400 --> 00:58:46.100
If it were me. I'd tell him.

970
00:58:47.000 --> 00:58:49.900
Couple of hours before we jump?

971
00:58:49.900 --> 00:58:52.500
I don't know.

972
00:59:01.800 --> 00:59:04.000
Why they springing 
these things on us now?

973
00:59:04.000 --> 00:59:07.300
It's just an extra 80 pounds 
strapped to your leg.

974
00:59:07.300 --> 00:59:12.300
Does anybody have any idea 
how the hell this thing works?

975
00:59:12.900 --> 00:59:15.600
Colonel Sink.

976
00:59:16.900 --> 00:59:19.500
Colonel Sink.

977
00:59:20.000 --> 00:59:22.200
"Soldiers of the regiment:

978
00:59:22.200 --> 00:59:24.900
tonight is the night

979
00:59:26.300 --> 00:59:27.500
of nights.

980
00:59:27.500 --> 00:59:31.200
Today. as you read this. 
you are en route

981
00:59:31.200 --> 00:59:34.100
to the great adventure for 
which you have trained for

982
00:59:34.100 --> 00:59:36.700
over two years."

983
00:59:36.700 --> 00:59:40.100
So. that's why they 
gave us ice cream.

984
00:59:42.000 --> 00:59:44.600
Easy company. listen up!

985
00:59:46.300 --> 00:59:49.800
Channel coast is socked 
in with rain and fog.

986
00:59:49.800 --> 00:59:51.500
No jump tonight.

987
00:59:51.900 --> 00:59:54.500
The invasion has 
been postponed.

988
00:59:54.500 --> 00:59:57.300
We're on a 24-hour 
stand-down.

989
01:00:00.600 --> 01:00:03.400
Well. this is quite a surprise.

990
01:00:03.400 --> 01:00:04.100
Not particularly.

991
01:00:04.100 --> 01:00:06.300
It so happens I rather expected it.

992
01:00:06.300 --> 01:00:10.800
Well. I can't see how you 
people can pass up $80.000

993
01:00:11.300 --> 01:00:12.900
for the cause.

994
01:00:13.400 --> 01:00:14.100
For whose cause?

995
01:00:14.100 --> 01:00:17.000
If you're so interested 
in serving a cause.

996
01:00:17.000 --> 01:00:18.700
why don't you join the army?

997
01:00:18.700 --> 01:00:21.400
Next. please.

998
01:00:24.500 --> 01:00:25.100
Oh. 4-m.

999
01:00:25.100 --> 01:00:26.500
You look 1-A to me.

1000
01:00:26.500 --> 01:00:29.800
Hey. you don't look 
so bad yourself.

1001
01:00:31.100 --> 01:00:32.000
"Dearest Johnny."

1002
01:00:32.000 --> 01:00:34.900
Well. should you 
be giving blood?

1003
01:00:34.900 --> 01:00:37.600
I woke up.

1004
01:00:38.100 --> 01:00:40.200
I got the wrong 
goddamn jacket.

1005
01:00:40.200 --> 01:00:40.900
Shh.

1006
01:00:40.900 --> 01:00:43.500
I was struck by lightning.

1007
01:00:50.900 --> 01:00:51.900
Nobody dancing.

1008
01:00:51.900 --> 01:00:53.800
It doesn't matter.

1009
01:00:54.100 --> 01:00:57.500
"Your pal. 
Bill Guarnere's brother..."

1010
01:02:30.200 --> 01:02:31.500
Good luck. lads.

1011
01:02:31.500 --> 01:02:32.900
See you. Tommy.

1012
01:02:32.900 --> 01:02:35.500
See you. mate.

1013
01:02:47.200 --> 01:02:50.500
Try and get these 
leg straps through.

1014
01:02:55.500 --> 01:02:58.200
Johnny?

1015
01:03:02.200 --> 01:03:04.900
Got something you 
might be looking for.

1016
01:03:04.900 --> 01:03:07.600
Took your jacket by mistake.

1017
01:03:07.600 --> 01:03:08.700
I'm sorry.

1018
01:03:08.700 --> 01:03:11.300
You read it?

1019
01:03:11.600 --> 01:03:13.800
Where the fuck 
is Monte Cassino?

1020
01:03:13.800 --> 01:03:15.100
I don't know.

1021
01:03:15.100 --> 01:03:17.700
Italy somewhere.

1022
01:03:19.100 --> 01:03:22.000
Sorry about your brother. Bill

1023
01:03:26.000 --> 01:03:28.600
He was. er...

1024
01:03:32.200 --> 01:03:34.800
Let's get this over with.

1025
01:03:37.900 --> 01:03:40.500
Bill?

1026
01:03:41.700 --> 01:03:44.700
I'll meet up with you over there.

1027
01:03:47.500 --> 01:03:51.200
Gentlemen. doc Roe is handing 
these out for air sickness.

1028
01:03:51.200 --> 01:03:53.300
Orders are. 
every man takes one now.

1029
01:03:53.300 --> 01:03:56.100
another 30 minutes in the air.

1030
01:03:57.000 --> 01:03:59.600
Lieutenant.

1031
01:04:04.100 --> 01:04:06.800
2nd platoon. listen up.

1032
01:04:09.900 --> 01:04:12.500
Good luck.

1033
01:04:13.000 --> 01:04:14.600
God bless you.

1034
01:04:15.400 --> 01:04:18.500
I'll see you in the 
assembly area.

1035
01:05:13.100 --> 01:05:14.200
If the wire constant is sensitive.

1036
01:05:14.200 --> 01:05:18.500
then I think all we should 
have to deal with is...

1037
01:05:22.900 --> 01:05:23.800
Goddamn. Lieb.

1038
01:05:23.800 --> 01:05:27.100
That airsick pill is 
making me loopy.

1039
01:10:13.500 --> 01:10:15.900
Subs cleaned up by 
Operations and Kungen
